;; The runtime's side of the modules whose Go package the host loads on their first import (queue 202e, the user's
;; decision on 202e's DECISION (a)): pyexpat (package arbace/pyexpat, over arbace/expat) is not linked into package py,
;; so a process that never imports it never loads expat's Go forms (about 2.8 s of goi's start). lazyModules names
;; each such module's namespace; SetPackageLoader is the host's callback that loads it (arbace.python.run requires the
;; namespace); the package's init registers the module in builtinModulesErr through RegisterBuiltinModule. A compiled
;; program (pyi's AOT) imports the packages itself, so their init has registered them before the first import.
;; The Ext* functions are the runtime's helpers such a package calls (package py's unexported names, unchanged).


